WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.502
White House Press Secretary
Sarah Huckabee Sanders

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:04.904
holds a lot of press briefings.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:08.207
But I, for one, don't think they
are asking all the questions

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:09.241
we need answers to.

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:10.744
So we decided to hold
another one

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.111
right here right now.
That's right.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:14.613
Sarah Huckabee Sanders
and the "Late Night" Press Corps

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:16.215
are here in our studio
and ready to go.

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:17.650
So without further ado,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.386
it's time for the "Late Night"
White House Press Briefing.

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.321
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:27.927 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.296
Sarah, Sarah, yes, over here.
Sarah.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.932
Sarah, Sarah, over here, yes,
thank you.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.734
Seth Meyers,
"Late Night with Seth Meyers."

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.170
Secretary Sanders,
when are you going

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.138
to start telling us the truth?

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:43.376
-Um, not today or tomorrow
or at any point ever.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.546
[ Laughter ]
-Great.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.913
Can you tell us a little bit

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:49.949
about Eric Trump's
birthday party?

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.851
-No one from the White House
staff will attend.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.120
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.590
-What did Jared Kushner
say to Donald Trump

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.758
during the election?

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.127
-I wish I could vote for you,
but I'm only 11.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.829
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:06.666
-Sarah, where do you see
yourself in five years?

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.167
-Further from the truth.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.403
[ Audience "ohhs", laughter ]

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.339
-President Trump
seems to be fairly unfriendly

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.540
to Angela Merkel.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.209
Was there ever a time
when Trump liked Germany?

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.879
-From 1942 to 1945.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:24.016
[ Audience groans,
scattered applause ]

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:27.920
[ Audience booing,
scattered applause ]

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:33.059
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:36.695
-Why does President Trump want
to meet with Vladimir Putin?

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:39.566
-To accept the check.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.433
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:44.704
-What did President Trump tell
his kids to do on Mother's Day?

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.138
-Call your moms.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:49.175
[ Audience groans, laughter ]

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.243
-The President has announced
a new branch

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:53.512
of the military called
the Space Force.

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:56.849
What's the first step
in getting that set up?

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:00.486
-We're gonna meet with
President Moon next week.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:06.492
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:10.563
-What does President Trump call
one jumping jack?

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.731
-The White House
Sports and Fitness Day.

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:16.602
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.504
-Sarah, be honest, do you ever

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:21.073
feel like you're
a little passive aggressive?

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.408
-I would be happy to answer it

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.777
if you would stop talking
long enough to let me do that.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.847
[ Audience groaning,
scattered laughter ]

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.215
-That was bad.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.283
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.686
-What is the line,
"My hump, my hump, my hump,

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.721
my lovely lady lumps" from?

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.923
-That is actually repeated
a number of times

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:39.392
throughout the Bible.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.893
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.062
-Oh, right.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.665
Take as much time as you need.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.200
You can answer
as long as you have to.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.870
Can you describe The President's
health regimen?

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.771
-Cake.

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:56.642
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.642 --> 00:03:00.379
So just cake?

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:02.081
What should I think about

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.083
when I'm trying to last longer
in the bedroom?

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.818
-Rudy Giuliani's love life.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:08.754
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yeah, that'll work.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:11.056
What is the best way
to win at table tennis?

00:03:11.056 --> 00:03:13.726
-Making sure that we no longer
allow China to play.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:17.964
-Yeah.
[ Audience groans, laughter ]

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.065
What did The President
say to his genitals

00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:21.934
before meeting
with Stormy Daniels?

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.403
-Happy birthday, Richard.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.003
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.003 --> 00:03:27.539
-Hey, you know what, uh,
your turn.

00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:29.108
Why don't you tell a joke?

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.010
-I work every single day

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.413
to give you accurate
and up to date information.

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:37.616
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That's fantastic.

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:39.385
That's a good one, Sarah. Yeah.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.320
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.888
Well, looks like
we are out of time.

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:43.990
So, on behalf of the rest

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.258
of the press corps,
have a good night.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.927
We'll be right back with
Benicio del Toro, everybody.

